# socks5.cfg.example
#
# Copy this next to Source.exe, rename it to  socks5.cfg , and fill it in.
# It is read only when you pick route [1] at startup.
#
# WARNING: this file holds a password in clear text. Keep it out of git and
# out of any shared folder. The repository's .gitignore already excludes
# socks5.cfg for that reason -- do not remove that line.
#
# Nothing here is compiled into the proxy. The password is never written to
# the log or printed to the console, including on the error paths.

# --- required ------------------------------------------------------------

host = 203.0.113.10
port = 1080
user = yourname
pass = yourpassword

# --- optional ------------------------------------------------------------

# Local port for the CONNECT shim the proxy opens for its own HTTP fetch.
# Change it only if something else already has this port.
# http_port = 18080

# --- what the server has to support --------------------------------------
#
# 1. Username/password authentication (RFC 1929). The proxy offers that
#    method and nothing else -- a server that would have taken it
#    anonymously is refused rather than silently used.
#
# 2. UDP ASSOCIATE (RFC 1928 section 7). The game session is UDP. Without
#    it the proxy starts, fetches the server list, and then reports that
#    the server will not do UDP.
#
#    On gost this is  metadata: udp: true  on the service.
#    On 3proxy and Dante it is on by default.
#
# --- what is routed, and what is not -------------------------------------
#
#   routed      the server_data.php fetch (TCP), and the ENet game session
#               (UDP), including the sub-server redirect after login.
#
#   NOT routed  the login page. The game client opens that itself, to the
#               'loginurl' address, and that request never reaches this
#               process -- the hosts file does not redirect it. It goes out
#               from this machine directly.
#
# So with this on, the login and the game session arrive from two different
# addresses. That is a real difference from playing normally, it is visible
# from the other side, and no setting here changes it. Read Docs/socks5.md
# before deciding whether that trade is one you want.
